## Help centre
help-eyebrow = Help
help-title = Help centre
help-lede = Short answers to common questions. Can’t find yours? Write to us.
help-meta-description = Answers about adding documents, voices, your own voice, your account and playback in Streams Reader.
help-toc-label = Topics
help-group-start = Getting started
help-group-voices = Voices and listening
help-group-account = Account and privacy
help-group-trouble = Fixing problems
help-q-add = How do I add something to listen to?
help-a-add = Open { $app }, choose Add, then paste a link, pick a file or paste text. It appears in your library, ready to play.
help-q-files = Which files work?
help-a-files = PDF, EPUB, Markdown, HTML and plain text files, web articles by link, and pasted text. Scanned PDFs without a text layer can’t be read yet.
help-q-play = How do I start from a certain sentence?
help-a-play = Tap the sentence in the reader, then choose Play from here.
help-q-install = How do I install it?
help-a-install = Add the web app to your home screen or dock. The steps for each device are on { $download }.
help-q-change-voice = How do I change the voice?
help-a-change-voice = Tap the voice name in the player and pick another. Reading continues from the current sentence.
help-q-expressive = Why is there a limit on expressive voices?
help-a-expressive = Expressive voices and your own voice run on shared graphics hardware with a daily budget. Everyone gets a fair share of it. Standard voices have no limit.
help-q-clone = How do I make my own voice?
help-a-clone = Go to Voices, choose Record your voice and read the eight lines shown. A quiet room and a steady distance from the microphone give the best result.
help-q-speed = Can I change the speed?
help-a-speed = Yes, from 0.5× to 3× in the player. The sleep timer is next to it.
help-q-account = Do I need an account?
help-a-account = Yes, so your library, voices and progress can follow you between devices. While we start out, accounts are by invitation.
help-q-data = What do you store about me?
help-a-data = Your email address, the documents you add, your listening progress and settings, and your voice recordings if you make a voice. The details are in our { $privacy } policy.
help-q-delete = How do I delete my data?
help-a-delete = Delete any document or voice in the app. To delete your whole account, write to { $email } from the address you signed up with.
help-q-stops = Playback stops when my screen turns off.
help-a-stops = Install the web app to your home screen and play from there. Some phones also stop background audio to save battery, so allow Streams Reader to run in the background.
help-q-no-audio = I pressed play and nothing happens.
help-a-no-audio = The first minute of a new document can take a few seconds to prepare. If it stays silent, check your connection and try again. Expressive voices may wait for the next daily share.
help-q-wrong-text = The text has extra bits, like menus or ads.
help-a-wrong-text = Some pages mix the article with other content. Paste the text directly instead, and tell us the link so we can improve the import.
help-contact-title = Still stuck?
help-contact-text = Write to us and a person will reply.

## Legal pages
legal-eyebrow = Legal
legal-updated = Last updated 30 October 2026.

privacy-title = Privacy
privacy-lede = What Streams Reader keeps, why, and how to remove it. Written to be read.
privacy-meta-description = What Streams Reader stores, who processes it, how long it is kept and how to delete it.
privacy-summary-title = In short
privacy-summary-1 = We keep what the app needs to read to you and to sync between your devices, nothing more. No ads, no trackers, no selling of data.
privacy-store-title = What we store
privacy-store-1 = Your account: your email address, used to sign in with a one-time code.
privacy-store-2 = Your library: the documents you add, your bookmarks, listening progress and settings.
privacy-store-3 = Audio: the speech made from your documents, kept so it plays instantly the next time.
privacy-store-4 = Your voice, if you make one: the recordings you read and the voice built from them. Only you can use it.
privacy-not-title = What we don’t do
privacy-not-1 = No advertising, no third-party analytics, no tracking pixels and no selling or sharing of your data for marketing.
privacy-not-2 = We don’t use your documents or recordings to train models.
privacy-processors-title = Who handles it
privacy-processors-1 = Cloudflare hosts the website and the app and stores documents and audio. Supabase stores accounts and sync data. Hugging Face runs the voice models that make the audio. Brevo sends sign-in emails.
privacy-processors-2 = Each of them processes data only to provide that service to us.
privacy-keep-title = How long we keep it
privacy-keep-1 = Your documents, progress and voice stay until you delete them or your account.
privacy-keep-2 = Audio made with standard voices is deleted automatically after 90 days and made again if you play it later.
privacy-cookies-title = Cookies and storage
privacy-cookies-1 = The app keeps you signed in and stores audio on your device so it plays again without downloading. This website sets no cookies.
privacy-rights-title = Your choices
privacy-rights-1 = You can see, export and delete your documents and voices in the app at any time.
privacy-rights-2 = To delete your account or ask anything about your data, write to { $email }. We answer within 30 days.
privacy-changes-title = Changes
privacy-changes-1 = If this policy changes, we update the date at the top and explain important changes in the app. The full history is on { $github }.

terms-title = Terms
terms-lede = The few rules for using Streams Reader, in plain words.
terms-meta-description = The terms for using Streams Reader: your content, your voice, fair use and the open-source licence.
terms-use-title = Using Streams Reader
terms-use-1 = Streams Reader is a free service for listening to text. You need an account, and while we start out accounts are by invitation.
terms-use-2 = Use it lawfully and don’t try to break, overload or get around its limits.
terms-content-title = Your content
terms-content-1 = What you add stays yours. Only add content you have the right to use, and keep listening to it personal.
terms-content-2 = We store and process your content only to read it to you, as described in the privacy policy.
terms-voices-title = Voices
terms-voices-1 = Make a voice only from your own recordings, or with clear permission from the person speaking.
terms-voices-2 = Don’t use any voice to deceive, impersonate, harass or commit fraud. We remove voices used this way.
terms-fair-title = Fair use
terms-fair-1 = Expressive voices share a daily budget. We may limit use that takes much more than a fair share, so everyone keeps access.
terms-open-title = Open source
terms-open-1 = The code is released under the MIT licence on { $github }. The voice models keep their own licences, listed on the credits page.
terms-warranty-title = No guarantees
terms-warranty-1 = The service is provided as it is, without warranties. It may change, pause or stop, and voices can mispronounce or misread text.
terms-warranty-2 = To the extent the law allows, we aren’t liable for indirect losses from using it.
terms-changes-title = Changes and contact
terms-changes-1 = We may update these terms and will show the date at the top. Questions go to { $email }.

